From 1ab964166a125b64ea4d5c05e7f5813bffd7bb2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:23:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] test(compression): pin the plugin observer contract at the
 local compaction boundary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#64231's verdict salvages #53806's compression lifecycle hook as an observer, and
#118382 asks for a plugin signal after compaction. Seven open PRs add a plugin hook
around context compaction, each with its own name and fire point. This test pins
the behaviour the one that lands should have, so it can be folded into that PR:

- a plugin subscribed to on_compression_complete is told exactly once per committed
  local compaction: rotated, in place, and the deferred manual /compress path once
  its host commits;
- when the callback runs, the compacted transcript is already durable in state.db
  under the session id it is handed;
- by then the attempt has released its commit fence and the session's compression
  lease. #118120 shows why: a memory-provider hook that blocked inside the fence
  left an interrupt waiting on the fence lock until the process was killed, and
  #127058 moves that hook out of the fence. A new plugin observer should not bring
  the hazard back;
- it is never told about an attempt that did not commit: a failed summary that
  aborts under compression.abort_on_summary_failure=true, the commit site's
  would-grow refusal, or a SessionDB write failure. The first two cases check the
  compressor's abort or refusal flag, and all three check that the session id and
  its state.db rows are unchanged before asserting silence;
- a manual compress whose host discards it is never announced either, even after a
  later finalize(committed=True). There the compacted rows are written (the case
  checks that), and only the host's discard keeps the callback silent;
- a raising subscriber and a directive-shaped return change neither the compacted
  messages nor the rebuilt system prompt.

Real AIAgent, SessionDB, ContextCompressor and CompressionCommitFence. Only the
summary LLM call (and the SessionDB write, for the commit failure) is replaced.
Agent init's model-metadata lookups are stubbed: the context window is pinned, and
the OpenRouter metadata prewarm thread runs a stub, so the test makes no network
request. The first test fails on main, which has no compression hook.

The payload and the delivery point follow designs from open PRs: the post-commit
boundary call of #53806, the post-compaction before/after token counts of #118847,
the in_place flag of #93391, and #127058's delivery after the fence is released.

